cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A Comprehensive R Container for Reproducible Bioinformatics Analysis on HPC Clusters in 2027"
message: "If you use this container in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Milner
    given-names: Andrew
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8313-913X
repository-code: https://github.com/armilner/r-bioinformatics-2027
abstract: >
  A ready-to-use R container for bioinformatics analysis. Covers single-cell
  RNA-seq (QC, ambient RNA, doublets, annotation, trajectories, cell-cell
  communication, CNV, VDJ), spatial deconvolution, bulk RNA-seq, methylation,
  ATAC-seq, and pathway enrichment, plus RStudio Server and Quarto. Built on
  R 4.6.1 with Bioconductor 3.23. Runs on HPC clusters through Apptainer or
  locally through Docker.
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - RNA-seq
  - methylation
  - ATAC-seq
  - R
  - container
  - reproducibility
